  <p>
    The builder's other methods are <code>grid</code>, <code>cellSize(size, {'{ gap, columnGap, rowGap }'})</code>,
    <code>symbols</code> (required), <code>weights</code>, <code>emptyId</code>,
    <code>inactive(cells, id?)</code>, <code>symbolData</code> (merged;
    <code>{'{ unmask: true }'}</code> is the headline use), <code>respins</code>,
    <code>lockAnimation</code>, <code>symbolZIndex</code>, <code>cellZIndex</code>,
    <code>speedProfile</code>, <code>speeds</code>, <code>initialSpeed</code>,
    <code>skipMode</code>, <code>stagger</code>, <code>anticipateWhen(fn)</code>,
    <code>cellChrome</code>, <code>cellMask</code>, <code>axis</code>,
    <code>ticker</code> (required) and <code>rng</code>. <code>build()</code>
    throws without <code>symbols</code> or <code>ticker</code>, or if
    <code>initialSpeed</code> names no registered profile.
  </p>

  <p>
    Board events, each with one object payload: <code>feature:enter</code>,
    <code>respin:start</code>, <code>cell:landed</code> (in stagger order),
    <code>coin:locked</code>, <code>coin:released</code>, <code>respins:changed</code>,
    <code>respin:end</code>, <code>board:full</code>, <code>feature:skip</code>,
    <code>feature:reset</code>, <code>feature:end</code>, <code>cells:activated</code>,
    <code>speed:changed</code>. Payloads are on the <a href="/architecture/events/">events page</a>.
    <code>HwCoin</code> is <code>{'{ readonly cell, readonly id, data? }'}</code>:
    the board owns <code>cell</code> and <code>id</code>, the game may mutate <code>data</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Nudge, in short</h2>

  <p>
    <code>ReelSet.nudge(reel, {'{ distance, direction, incoming, duration?, ease?, startDelay?, signal? }'})</code>
    moves one reel at rest by <code>distance</code> cells (a positive integer
    below the strip capacity) in <code>'forward'</code> or <code>'reverse'</code>
    relative to the reel's own axis, feeding <code>incoming</code> (length must
    equal <code>distance</code>, in start-to-end order, may overflow into the
    buffers). Defaults: <code>duration = 200 × distance</code> ms,
    <code>ease = 'power2.out'</code> with overshoot clamped. It throws while a
    spin, refill or expand step is in flight, on a reel with
    <code>bufferEnd === 0</code>, or if any pin is on that reel; while a nudge
    runs, <code>spin</code>, <code>setResult</code>, <code>pin</code>,
    <code>setShape</code> and resizing throw. Events: <code>nudge:start</code>
    (after pre-placement), then <code>nudge:complete</code> with the new
    <code>symbols</code>, or <code>nudge:cancelled</code> with a reason and an
    <code>AbortError</code> rejection. The per-reel bus gets
    <code>phase:enter('nudge')</code> and <code>phase:exit('nudge')</code>.
    <code>skipNudge(reel?)</code> fast-forwards and still resolves normally.
    It is per reel by design; run several with <code>Promise.all</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Presenting wins</h2>

  <div class="not-prose my-6 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-3">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-4">
      <div class="text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-1">WinPresenter</div>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/80"><code>wins/WinPresenter.ts</code>. <code>show(wins)</code> aborts any previous run, sorts by value (<code>sortByValue: true</code>), emits <code>win:start</code>, then per win per cycle dims losers (<code>dimLosers</code> alpha <code>0.35</code>), emits <code>win:group</code>, then <code>win:symbol</code> per cell spaced by <code>stagger</code> (0) and plays <code>symbolAnim</code> (<code>'win'</code>, a named animation, or a function). <code>cycleGap</code> 400 ms, <code>cycles</code> 1 (<code>-1</code> infinite). <code>win:end</code> fires in <code>finally</code>. In a cascade, call it from <code>presentWinners</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-4">
      <div class="text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-1">SymbolSpotlight</div>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/80"><code>reelSet.spotlight</code>. <code>show(positions)</code> emits <code>spotlight:start</code>, dims the viewport (<code>dimAmount</code> 0.5), reparents each view into <code>viewport.spotlightContainer</code> (<code>promoteAboveMask</code> true), and awaits <code>playWin()</code> (<code>playWinAnimation</code> true). <code>hide()</code> reparents back, skipping views the pool recycled, and emits <code>spotlight:end</code>. <code>cycle(lines)</code> shows each for <code>displayDuration</code> 2000 ms with <code>gapDuration</code> 300 ms, <code>cycles</code> 1.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-4">
      <div class="text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-1">promote()</div>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/80"><code>ReelSet.promote(positions) → release</code> is the non-reparenting alternative. It attaches the views to <code>viewport.promotedLayer</code> (a RenderLayer), prunes itself on <code>symbol:created</code> when a swap hands the cell a new instance, and does no dim and no <code>playWin</code>. The engine never computes or draws wins (ADR 007); a <code>Win</code> is <code>{'{ cells, value?, kind?, id? }'}</code> and the order of <code>cells</code> matters when <code>stagger &gt; 0</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

